<%/* Admin: system-wide metadata refresh.

     Mirrors the indexer admin page in layout — one polled status
     panel + one action area, both server-rendered. The status panel
     itself surfaces the Start / Cancel buttons depending on whether
     there's an active batch. */%>
<h1 class="page-title">Metadata Refresh</h1>
<p class="page-subtitle">
    Re-fetch metadata from ArchivesSpace for every active object and
    collection. Runs in the background — paced so on-demand refreshes
    (kebab → "Refresh metadata") still get priority and are never
    starved by a long bulk job. Per-row failures retry up to
    <code>METADATA_MAX_ATTEMPTS</code> times before landing in the
    dead-letter set, where they're available for inspection but no
    longer consume worker capacity.
</p>

<div class="content-card">
    <div class="content-card-header">
        <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0;">Status</h2>
        <div class="control-group">
            <span class="htmx-indicator">
                <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm text-muted" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <%/* Poll every 2s. The status query is two small indexed reads
         (the batch row + an activity snapshot capped at 13 rows
         total) so this is cheap, and 2s is the cadence that makes
         "currently fetching" feel real-time even at the worker's
         ~12-row/min steady state.

         Critically, the Start/Cancel buttons live INSIDE this
         polled region. Without intervention, a polling tick mid-
         confirm-modal would swap the partial — the original button
         DOM detaches — and the confirm modal's proceed-click on
         the orphaned button no-ops.
         dashboard.js solves this with an htmx:beforeRequest hook
         that aborts polling requests (any element whose hx-trigger
         contains `every`) while `body.htmx-confirm-pending` is set.
         We don't use hx-trigger's `[filter-expr]` syntax because
         htmx evaluates it via new Function(), which our CSP
         (script-src without 'unsafe-eval') correctly forbids. */%>
    <div id="metadata-refresh-status"
         hx-get="<%= dashboard_base %>/admin/metadata-refresh/status"
         hx-trigger="load, every 2s"
         hx-swap="innerHTML">
        <div class="text-muted small p-3">Loading…</div>
    </div>
</div>
